{"ticker":"AZO","name":"AutoZone","sector":"Consumer Discretionary","industry":"Automotive Retail","exchange":null,"index":null,"cik":866787,"as_of":"2026-11-19T03:44:36Z","reasons":["top_idea"],"profile":{"summary":"AutoZone, Inc. operates as a retailer and distributor of automotive replacement parts and accessories in the Americas. The company offers a product line for cars, sport utility vehicles, vans, and light duty trucks, including new and remanufactured automotive hard parts, maintenance items, accessories, and non-automotive products. It also provides failure products, such as A/C compressors, batteries and accessories, bearings, belts and hoses, calipers, chassis, clutches, CV axles, engines, fuel pumps, fuses, ignition, lighting, mufflers, radiators, starters and alternators, thermostats, tire repair, and water pumps. In addition, the company offers maintenance products, including antifreeze and windshield washer fluid; brake drums, rotors, shoes, and pads; chemicals, including brake and power steering fluid, and oil and fuel additives; oil and transmission fluid; oil, cabin, air, fuel, and transmission filters; oxygen sensors; paint and accessories; refrigerant and accessories; shock absorbers and struts; spark plugs and wires; and windshield wipers. Further, it provides air fresheners, cell phone accessories, drinks and snacks, floor mats and seat covers, interior and exterior accessories, mirrors, performance products protectants and cleaners, sealants and adhesives, steering wheel covers, tools, towing, vehicle entertainment systems, and wash and wax. It offers its products under the AutoZone, AutoZone Rewards, Get in the Zone, Zone, Duralast, Econocraft, ProElite, ProVantage, ShopPro, SureBilt, TotalPro, TruGrade, Valucraft, and ALLDATA names. The company sells its products through stores, www.autozone.com, www.autozonepro.com, www.alldata.com, and www.duralastparts.com, as well as commercial sales program that provides delivery of parts and other products and commercial credit to local, regional and national repair garages, dealers, service stations, fleet owners, and other accounts. AutoZone, Inc. was founded in 1979 and is headquartered in Memphis, Tennessee.","website":"https://www.autozone.com","employees":79200,"hq":"Memphis, TN","currency":"USD","fx":null},"quote":{"price":3308.69,"mcap":53251200000.0,"ev":66076000000.0,"low52":2730.65,"high52":3996.25,"beta":0.373,"shares":16094300.0,"pe":21.6892,"fpe":17.2228,"eps":152.55,"feps":192.111,"div_yield":0.0},"street":{"low":3000.0,"mean":3656.62,"high":4450.0,"rec":1.53571,"rec_key":"buy","analysts":24.0},"officers":[{"name":"Mr. William C. Rhodes III","title":"Executive Chairman","age":60,"pay":null,"fiscal_year":2022},{"name":"Mr. Philip B. Daniele III","title":"CEO, President & Director","age":56,"pay":2942370.0,"fiscal_year":2022},{"name":"Mr. Thomas B. Newbern","title":"Chief Operating Officer","age":63,"pay":1800860.0,"fiscal_year":2022},{"name":"Mr. Eric S. Gould","title":"Executive Vice President of Merchandising, Marketing, Supply Chain","age":56,"pay":981173.0,"fiscal_year":2022},{"name":"Mr. Kenneth E. Jaycox Jr.","title":"Senior VP of Commercial","age":57,"pay":890078.0,"fiscal_year":2022},{"name":"Mr. John Scott Murphy","title":"Principal Accounting Officer, VP & Controller","age":52,"pay":null,"fiscal_year":2022},{"name":"Ms. Michelle K. Borninkhof","title":"Senior VP & Chief Information Officer","age":51,"pay":null,"fiscal_year":2022},{"name":"Mr. Brian L. Campbell","title":"Vice President of Tax, Treasury & Investor Relations","age":null,"pay":null,"fiscal_year":2022},{"name":"Ms. Jennifer M. Bedsole","title":"Senior VP, General Counsel & Secretary","age":54,"pay":null,"fiscal_year":2022},{"name":"Mr. Eric J. Leef","title":"Senior Vice President of Human Resources","age":51,"pay":null,"fiscal_year":2022}],"ownership":{"insiders_pct":0.00429,"institutions_pct":0.97181,"institutions_count":1716.0,"top_holders":[{"holder":"Blackrock Inc.","pct"